### Defect found and fixed while validating the Puppet implementation ###

SYMPTOM
  Driving the portal through the nginx reverse proxy with a real browser,
  rather than curl against the health endpoint, broke at the first
  redirect. Submitting the login form landed on
      http://127.0.0.1/attendance/login?error    <- the port is missing
  and the browser reported ERR_CONNECTION_REFUSED.

CAUSE
  Both the Ansible and the Puppet nginx template carried
      proxy_set_header Host $host;
  nginx's $host is the normalised host WITHOUT the port. Spring Security
  builds its redirect Location headers from the Host header it receives,
  so every 302 the application issued pointed at port 80. The health
  endpoint never redirects, which is why every curl check in Stages 13
  and 14 passed and the defect survived undetected.

FIX
      proxy_set_header Host $http_host;
  $http_host is the client's Host header verbatim, port included.
  Applied to BOTH implementations, since both shared the defect:
      ansible/roles/nginx/templates/attendance.conf.j2
      puppet/modules/attendance/templates/nginx-attendance.conf.epp

VERIFICATION 1 -- an unauthenticated GET /dashboard must redirect to
/login on the SAME port the request arrived on:
  Ansible node (:8200) -> Location: http://127.0.0.1:8200/attendance/login
  Puppet  node (:8300) -> Location: http://127.0.0.1:8300/attendance/login

VERIFICATION 2 -- the full login flow through the proxy, both nodes.
The script asserts it reaches /dashboard, so it fails loudly if the
regression ever returns (puppet/lab/browse-node.sh):
  Ansible node (:8200)
    /login       -> http://127.0.0.1:8200/attendance/login             rows=5    Sign in · Attendance Portal
    login submit -> http://127.0.0.1:8200/attendance/dashboard
    /attendance  -> http://127.0.0.1:8200/attendance/attendance        rows=10   Attendance records · Attendance Portal
    /students    -> http://127.0.0.1:8200/attendance/students          rows=10   Student roll · Attendance Portal
    /review      -> http://127.0.0.1:8200/attendance/review            rows=30   Review queue · Attendance Portal
  Puppet node (:8300)
    /login       -> http://127.0.0.1:8300/attendance/login             rows=5    Sign in · Attendance Portal
    login submit -> http://127.0.0.1:8300/attendance/dashboard
    /attendance  -> http://127.0.0.1:8300/attendance/attendance        rows=10   Attendance records · Attendance Portal
    /students    -> http://127.0.0.1:8300/attendance/students          rows=10   Student roll · Attendance Portal
    /review      -> http://127.0.0.1:8300/attendance/review            rows=30   Review queue · Attendance Portal

Both reach /dashboard on the correct port and render live seeded data.
